<title>UK: Russian straight-run fuel oil well supplied in NWE.</title>
<headline>Russian straight-run fuel oil well supplied in NWE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian high sulphur straight-run fuel oil was well supplied in northern Europe on Monday, while low sulphur markets were quiet, traders said.</p>
<p>A Russian M-40 cargo was sold at around $3 premium to the mean of the two cracked fuel oil quotes, while full E-4 grade was talked around $3 premium to the E-4 formula. Very prompt cargoes were talked at a discount to that.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
